+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P1] Guardian verdict executor missing: 3 evaluated PRs stuck open, escalation channel idle (bridge-20261027-guardian-verdict-executor)
+
+## Problem
+The PR Guardian evaluates verdicts but nothing enacts them. Verified live 2026-10-25 via `guardian_sweep` + `github_list_prs`:
+
+- PR #328 and #326: verdict `CLOSE_PR` ("no measurable improvement evidenced") — both still **open** since Oct 23–24
+- PR #324: verdict `FIX_REGRESSION_THEN_MERGE` (improvementScore −7.5; regressed `debug_artifacts`, `type_suppressions`) — no follow-up work order generated
+- `guardian_act` exists as a tool but was never invoked on these PRs
+- The Telegram alerts bot (`telegram-primary`, healthy) sent nothing about any of this — the escalation lane is wired but silent
+
+Meanwhile the Bridge Intake workflow itself failed twice recently (runs #307/#308), starving the same pipeline this executor is meant to drain. (CI failure-masking root cause is separately tracked in #1326/#1258 — this order is about the **verdict→action** gap only.)
+
+## Impact (AIQ mapping)
+- AIQ-049: system cannot claim it "clearly reports done/failed" when verdicts decay into stale PRs
+- AIQ-070: human oversight exists but the auto-lane it depends on is half-duplex (evaluate ✓, enact ✗)
+- AIQ-123: incident/escalation process demonstrably not wired end-to-end
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change)
+1. Add a scheduled "verdict executor" step to the Bridge Intake workflow: after `guardian_sweep`, call `guardian_act` with `decision: auto` for each evaluated PR (Tier-2 only; Tier-3 always lands in HITL approvals per existing policy).
+2. Wire `notify_telegram` on: every enacted verdict, every `ESCALATE_TO_ADMIN`, and every red CI run.
+3. Emit one work order per `FIX_REGRESSION_THEN_MERGE` verdict automatically (title prefixed with the PR number).
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] After one sweep cycle: PRs #326 and #328 are closed with Guardian commentary; #324 has a spawned fix work order
+- [ ] Telegram message received for each enacted verdict
+- [ ] No Tier-3 PR is ever auto-acted (assert in workflow log)
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** evaluation without enactment is dead weight; stale PRs also skew future Guardian baselines.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) manual enactment — violates the autonomy design and will rot again; (b) deleting the guardian_act tool path — removes governed authority that already has HITL guardrails.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P1-high` `area:guardian` `AIQ:049` `AIQ:070` `AIQ:123`
